      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original using its own earlier source/glossary preparation, isolated from the other proposal. The shared-viewing object becomes the spirit's exclusive object of experience; the negative three-part-existence condition is distinct from the lexical exclusive compound. Blta bya owns the explicit look in the expanded nominal/verbal construction and thun mong ba owns shared; object and together remain unwrapped reprises. The single lag tu blangs has a documented discontinuous HGM gloss, picks up ... in his hand: separate lag/hand, tu/in and blangs/picks up preserve it without capturing supplied the glass or his. First de'i tshe na owns When, second owns at this point; first skye ba owns exists, second starts being. Khyad chos owns different parts; gsum owns the later three, not the supplied earlier three different beings. The causal yin pas owns Since as a complete d3 connective, not as a broken suffix. Gang po has no separate fullness exponent; phyi ma and the expanded de ltar/de anaphora are omitted as distributed or expanded wording. Rnag/khrag members remain inside the terminal compound; glossary reciprocal alternatives are disclosed. Exact C15:412/C16:843/C18:1126 fields and P7:22's English match do not prove independent publication or ingestion history. No source or glossary edits."
